{"kind":"report","text":"Corrected Stage 3 readiness report for request #4050 on promise c27bc512, answering assert 61e91aba; it replaces report b180feed. Owning head is current main e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c; every reference in the attachment is a full repository path with a line checked at that head. The three cited normaliser, test and decision files are byte-identical to the earlier review head e93505c9.\n\n1. Evidence scope. I examined the repository (notes, docs, bundle, git log --all) and, this time, the tailapp workroom log itself: all 2,528 statements scanned for stage 3, url-capture, url-reputation and reputation companion. Every stage 3 match belongs to the MCP catalog or value-codec features. The URL-capture lineage (#2187 start, Stage 1 design to approval #2274, revival merged #2702, Stage 2 approved #3024 and merged #3026, umbrella closed #3108, recovery backport #3960 to #3983) contains no request, promise, assert or report that assigns, schedules or defers URL Stage 3. The requester's through-#4049 audit is corroboration, not the basis.\n\n2. Citations. All abbreviated references are expanded; the attachment and its previews resolve at e3ad5f92.\n\n3. Normaliser gap, reproduced through the real evaluator in a scratch checkout at this head, left clean. tailapps/url-reputation/folds/normalize.jsonata lines 19 and 26 to 28 bind the host by scheme-plus-host prefix and admit a colon at the boundary. Results: https://user:pw@example.com/path with host example.com is rejected; https://example.com:pw@evil.test/path with host example.com is admitted; the same URL with its true host evil.test is rejected; https://example.com:8443@evil.test/path with host example.com is admitted; the plain control is admitted. So a correct adapter loses every observation carrying userinfo, and a wrong host is bound whenever the supplied host is followed by a colon. The existing test at tailapps/url_reputation_test.go line 143 covers only a no-colon spoof. Stage 3 therefore needs a bounded bundle correction: parse the authority (after the scheme, up to the first slash, question mark or hash; keep the part after the last at-sign; strip a numeric port) and compare it exactly to the supplied host, keeping observed_full unmodified and the host-shape rule intact, with the five cases above added as tests. No recovery backport copy of the normaliser exists at this head, so one file changes. It is a same-runtime bundle source change with unchanged table shapes; whether an installed Tailapp continues or resets is governed by docs/reference/resident-upgrade.md and is not inferred here. The unconditional two-script-trees-only scope is withdrawn; recommend landing the correction as its own small request before Stage 3.\n\nEverything else stands: minimal source-only scope with no internal/ change beyond the bundle; external contracts unchanged with the Codex hook-trust step and the undocumented WebSearch response shape as the two gaps; decisions for Hugh are the Stage 3 assignment, the normaliser correction's placement, the six-versus-five bundle catalog, Codex hook trust wording, WebSearch scope, and the Web Risk URL refresh. Stage 3 implementation and Stage 4 documentation remain outstanding; this review cannot mark the feature delivered.","body":{"corrects":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:b180feed9b4e82b2a1431c90da46bdc6db4d12f5","head":"e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c","normalizer_gap":"confirmed","stage3_assigned":"none-found","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:61e91aba0321726268411ddbc065edd24b1e754b, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:c27bc5125a753dc28233ddeaa0376a7db87f7980 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:4472b3ba65a898d310f6225632b8a5528fbf437a, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:6c172daedfcbd0033a345a0ff0562c0988dae142, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d